From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Report legacy OpenGL contexts when an alternative is offered.

A legacy context is OpenGL 2.1 on macOS. An application that needs a newer
compatibility profile fails soon after creating one, often without any
error Wine can see. When RUNEON_GFX_DIR_MESAGL is set, report once per
process that a legacy context was requested, and once that a core context
was requested, as loaders that bootstrap with a legacy context then do. A
launcher can then tell a start that failed on the legacy context from other
failures. The lines are reported on request, not on success, after the
existing attribute and version checks; requests those checks refuse report
nothing. win32u's internal pbuffer contexts also count as legacy. The
lines are diagnostics only: without the variable nothing is printed, and
context creation is unchanged either way.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index 8f24ef5..9b7a8b9 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2216,6 +2216,28 @@ static BOOL macdrv_context_create(int format, void *shared, const int *attrib_li
         return FALSE;
     }
 
+    /* Runeon: a legacy context is OpenGL 2.1 on macOS, which applications
+     * that need a newer compatibility profile cannot use. When the launcher
+     * offers an alternative, say once per process that one was created, and
+     * once that a core context followed (as loaders that bootstrap with a
+     * legacy context do), so a failed start can be attributed. Reported on
+     * request, not on success; win32u's internal pbuffer contexts also count
+     * as legacy. */
+    if (getenv("RUNEON_GFX_DIR_MESAGL"))
+    {
+        static BOOL legacy_reported, core_reported;
+        if (!core && !legacy_reported)
+        {
+            legacy_reported = TRUE;
+            FIXME("runeon-gl-legacy-context: legacy context limited to OpenGL 2.1\n");
+        }
+        else if (core && !core_reported)
+        {
+            core_reported = TRUE;
+            FIXME("runeon-gl-core-context: core context %d.%d\n", major, minor);
+        }
+    }
+
     if (!(context = calloc(1, sizeof(*context)))) return FALSE;
 
     context->format = format;
